# en -> de
#
# Page-title catalogue for the pages: tree of ImplementationGuide-mii-ig-dokument.json.
#
# WHAT THESE UNITS DO (verified on IG Publisher 2.2.11): they localize the
# BREADCRUMBS of translated pages -- including the root label "Inhaltsverzeichnis"
# -- and the browser <title> tag. Where no unit exists the publisher copies the
# default-language title into every language.
#
# WHAT THEY DO NOT DO:
#   * The BODY of toc.html (the generated hierarchy table) is NOT localized. The
#     German toc.html renders "2.1 Guidance for Researchers" in English although
#     the unit below supplies "Anleitung fuer Forschende" and the breadcrumb on
#     that same page is German. Publisher limitation, NOT a missing unit -- adding
#     or regenerating units will not change it.
#   * The left-hand/top NAVIGATION MENU is not driven by these units. Its German
#     comes from input/translations/<lang>/includes/menu.xml.
#
# An empty msgstr means UNTRANSLATED: that entry falls back to en.
#
# HOW TO UPDATE after a change to the pages: tree -- either way works:
#   (a) By hand: run 'sushi .', walk definition.page in
#       fsh-generated/resources/ImplementationGuide-mii-ig-dokument.json
#       recursively INCLUDING the root page (its title is "Table of Contents"),
#       and keep one unit per distinct title, msgid copied byte for byte.
#   (b) With the generator gen-page-title-po.py. It is NOT part of this
#       repository. It is published in the skill catalog
#       https://github.com/forschungsgruppe-digital-health/agent-skills, skill
#       'mii-ig-migration', at
#       skills/mii-ig-migration/scripts/gen-page-title-po.py -- obtain it there.
#       It regenerates non-destructively: units it does not own (the IG's own
#       title/description/publisher, per-artifact units, a gettext header entry)
#       are kept verbatim, and a non-empty msgstr below survives and wins over
#       the seed.
# Full recipe: docs/recipes/add-translation.md, sections 5a-5c.
#
# Requires 'de' in BOTH an i18n-lang and a translation-sources parameter of
# sushi-config.yaml -- a language missing from translation-sources has its .po
# files silently ignored.

